  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/Marrickville/Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 14 Unique Environmental Features.pdf\n\nClause 2.14 - other (development_control): The following  objectives, controls and design solutions apply to land that contains unique environmental features. Additional objectives and controls also apply to land in the Thornley  Street Scenic Protection Area.\n\nClause 2.14.2 - other (development_control): Development must be designed to address any distinctive environmental features of the s ite or on adjoining nearby land.\n\nClause 2.14.2 - other (development_control): Development must  respond to these features by appropriately considering outlook, the location of  structures , design  and materials.\n\nClause 2.14.2 - height_limit (development_control): Development adjoining public open space must be set back from open space and be of a height and scale  appropriate to the unique environmental qualities of the area.\n\nClause 2.14.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Clearing of vegetation must be minimised and colours and materials selected that integrate with the characteristics of the area.\n\nClause 2.14.3 - other (development_control): The Thornley Street scenic protection area is an area with unique environmental features and has been identified for its landscape, cultural and scenic qualities.\n\nClause 2.14.5 - other (development_control): Development  within the scenic protection area must be : \ni. Designed and located to minimise potential adverse environme ntal impact.\n\nClause 2.14.5 - other (development_control): Of a scale compatible with the character, landscape and scenic qualities of the area\n\n",
